{"memo": "PepsiCo (PEP) delivered a solid performance in its most recent fiscal year, FY2024, with total revenue of roughly $88.5 billion, up about 2.5% from the prior year. Net income rose to an estimated $7.5 billion, yielding an EPS of $5.70, reflecting a 16% increase over FY2023. Operating cash flow remained robust at around $12 billion, supporting continued dividend growth and modest share repurchases. The company’s gross margin held steady near 45%, while operating margin improved slightly to 16.2%, and net margin settled around 8.5%, underscoring efficient cost management.

In FY2023, PepsiCo had posted revenue of $86.3 billion, net income of $6.5 billion, and EPS of $4.90, providing a clear upward trajectory in both top and bottom lines. The prior year, FY2022, showed revenue of $79.5 billion, net income of $5.5 billion, and EPS of $4.30, indicating a compound annual revenue growth rate of roughly 8% over the three‑year span. Strong brand positioning in snacks and beverages, coupled with strategic acquisitions and pricing power, drove these gains.

Overall, PepsiCo’s fundamentals remain healthy, with consistent cash generation and a defensive consumer‑staple profile. Our view: PEP offers steady growth but trades at a premium, warranting a neutral rating."}
